<title>CANADA: Poco Pete Q4 share net climbs from loss.</title>
<headline>Poco Pete Q4 share net climbs from loss.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr	 Profit	C$0.15     Loss	C$0.02</p>
<p> Net	 Profit	17,770     Loss	 1,959</p>
<p> Cash flow/shr	     0.64		     0.31</p>
<p> Revs		     155,200		   67,776</p>
<p>	   YEAR</p>
<p> Shr	 Profit	C$0.30   Profit	C$0.05</p>
<p> Net	 Profit	34,356   Profit	 4,298</p>
<p> Cash flow/shr	     2.02		     1.43</p>
<p> Revs		     471,580		  274,420</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 114,595		   94,452</p>
<p>   (All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Note: Per share and shares outstanding figures above are in basic terms. Poco's fully diluted cash flow per share for the fourth quarter was C$0.61 in 1996 and C$0.30 in 1995. Full year cash flow per share was C$1.93 in 1996 and C$1.36 in 1995. The company reported 121.8 million average fully diluted shares outstanding in 1996 and 105.2 million the year before.</p>
<p>Company full name is Poco Petroleums Ltd.</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
